# Line-ending policy: everything text is LF in the repository.
#
# HISTORY: this file previously relied on `* text=lf`, which is a NO-OP — `lf` is not
# a valid value for the `text` attribute (git accepts set / unset / `auto` and treats
# anything else as undefined), so it fell through to core.autocrlf. Only the explicit
# `eol=lf` lines ever worked, which is why .cs warned on CRLF while .md silently took
# 2276 CR bytes into WORKSPACE/DISCOVERIES.md on 2026-08-05.
#
# NOTE: engine/.gitattributes carries the same policy and MUST be kept in sync — a
# deeper .gitattributes wins per-attribute, so anything set only here is inert for
# every path under engine/.

# Catch-all: auto-detect text vs binary, normalize text to LF in the repo. This is
# what covers EXTENSIONLESS files (Makefile, openra, pre-commit, COPYING, AUTHORS,
# VERSION) and any new file type nobody remembers to list below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats — pinned explicitly so content auto-detection can never misfire on
# a game asset or an image. This is NOT belt-and-braces: engine/packaging/artwork
# PNGs legitimately contain CR bytes (ra_16x16.png is 632 bytes with 5 CRs), and
# normalizing one strips a byte and corrupts the image.
*.shp binary
*.aud binary
*.des binary
*.jun binary
*.tem binary
*.sno binary
*.int binary
*.tmp binary
*.pal binary
*.bin binary
*.mix binary
*.dat binary
*.win binary
*.oramap binary
*.a00 binary
*.a01 binary
*.a02 binary
*.a03 binary
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.ttf binary

# Custom for Visual Studio
*.cs     diff=csharp
